   * registration email verification process.
   *
   * This operation allows sellers who have registered but haven't verified
   * their email address to request a new verification email if they didn't
   * receive the original or if the previous token has expired. The system
   * validates the seller's authenticated identity through their JWT token, then
   * checks that their account status is either 'pending_verification' or
   * 'pending_approval'. When validated, the system generates a new
   * cryptographically secure verification token with a 24-hour expiration
   * period, updates the database record, and sends a new verification email
   * with the new token.
   *
   * Security: This operation requires a valid seller authentication token.
   * Sellers who have already been approved, rejected, or suspended cannot
   * trigger this operation. Rate limiting is applied to prevent abuse of the
   * resend functionality. Email verification tokens are single-use and have a
   * 24-hour expiration window. The email contains a secure link that validates
   * the token and updates the seller account status to 'pending_approval'.
   *
   * Related operations: POST /auth/register (initial registration), POST
   * /auth/login (account authentication), PATCH /sellers/approve (administrator
   * approval of seller registration).
   *
   * @param connection
   * @x-autobe-specification Verify seller identity from JWT token. Check that seller exists with status 'pending_verification' or 'pending_approval'. Confirm email verification token exists and is expired or not yet used. Generate new verification token with 24-hour expiration. Update database record with new token and timestamp. Send new verification email containing the token. Return 204 No Content on success. Return 400 if seller status is not pending, 401 if token is invalid, 403 if seller has been approved/rejected/suspended, and 429 if rate limited.
   * @nestia Generated by Nestia - https://github.com/samchon/nestia
   */
  @TypedRoute.Post("resend")
  public async resend(
    @SellerAuth()
    seller: SellerPayload,
  ): Promise<void> {
    try {
      return await postShoppingMallSellerAuthSellersEmailResend({
        seller,
      });
    } catch (error) {
      console.log(error);
      throw error;
    }
  }
}

