  /**
   * Retrieve aggregated performance metrics for the authenticated seller's shop
   * on the shoppingMall platform.
   *
   * This performance dashboard operation calculates key business indicators
   * based on historical order and sales data captured via the platform's
   * snapshot principle. All metrics are computed from immutable order snapshots
   * that preserve the exact state of products, variants, seller profiles, and
   * pricing at the moment of purchase, ensuring historical accuracy. The
   * calculation excludes any products or variants that have been deleted by the
   * seller after the order was placed, as these are not reflected in the order
   * snapshots.
   *
   * Performance metrics are updated in real-time as new orders are completed,
   * and all data is sourced directly from the system's finalized order records
   * and product snapshots. Notably, due to the snapshot principle, a seller's
   * current product price changes or inventory levels do not affect the
   * historical performance data — the metrics reflect the actual transaction
   * conditions at the time of sale.
   *
   * The revenue figure includes only completed payments and excludes refunds or
   * cancellations. The average order value and number of customers represent
   * unique customers who completed any purchase from the seller's shop.
   * Customer retention is calculated based on repeat purchase behavior, defined
   * as customers making more than one purchase.
   *
   * This endpoint is accessible only to authenticated sellers and is never
   * available to customers or administrators, preserving data privacy and
   * adhering to role-based access controls as defined in the platform
   * specifications.
   *
   * Related operations: GET /products — for individual product performance; GET
   * /orders — for detailed order inspection; GET /inventory — for current stock
   * levels.
   *
   * @param connection
   * @x-autobe-specification Query shopping_mall_sale_view_stats to extract total sales and revenue for the authenticated seller's account. Join with shopping_mall_orders to count total orders and unique customer IDs. Join with shopping_mall_products and shopping_mall_sellers to ensure only active (non-deleted) products are included. Compute average order value by dividing total revenue by total orders. Calculate customer retention rate as: (customers with multiple orders / total customers) * 100. Sum all order item quantities to determine total units sold. Aggregate all metrics in a single query with grouping. Cache results for 5 minutes using seller ID as cache key. Return a single aggregated record with all performance fields. Apply pagination only if extended reports are requested in future.
   * @nestia Generated by Nestia - https://github.com/samchon/nestia
   */
  @TypedRoute.Get()
  public async index(
    @SellerAuth()
    seller: SellerPayload,
  ): Promise<IShoppingMallSaleSnapshot> {
