   *   format). This parameter identifies the specific item to cancel within the
   *   order.
   * @x-autobe-specification Update the status of the specified order item to 'cancelled' in the shopping_mall_order_items table. Create an inventory record using the inventory service to add back the quantity of the item to the variant's stock, with reason 'admin_cancellation' and source_id as this order item's ID. Log the administrative action in the audit service with admin ID, order ID, order item ID, and timestamp. Immediately update the order's overall status if all items are cancelled. Return 204 No Content on success. Validate that the authenticated user is an admin. Validate that the order item exists and belongs to the specified order. Reject if order item is already cancelled or refunded. Handle concurrent modifications with optimistic locking.
   * @nestia Generated by Nestia - https://github.com/samchon/nestia
   */
  @TypedRoute.Post()
  public async erase(
    @AdminAuth()
    admin: AdminPayload,
    @TypedParam("orderId")
    orderId: string & tags.Format<"uuid">,
    @TypedParam("orderItemId")
    orderItemId: string & tags.Format<"uuid">,
